[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [b]AlienX's Mod Loader[/b] first[/*]
[*]Extract the Mod Loader into
[code]StarRupture/Binaries/Win64/[/code]
[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapExtension_Plugin.dll[/b] and [b]MapExtension_Plugin.json[/b] from the client archive into
[code]StarRupture/Binaries/Win64/Plugins/[/code]
[/*]
[*]Start the game once so the plugin can initialize and generate its config file[/*]
[*]Place [b]MapExtensionViewer.html[/b], [b]map-tiles[/b], and [b]map-data[/b] together wherever you want on your PC[/*]
[*]Double-click [b]MapExtensionViewer.html[/b] to open it in your default browser[/*]
[*]Keep the game running while you use the map viewer[/*]
[/list]

[b]Install from the client archive, not from the standalone DLL file.[/b] The archive also contains [b]MapExtension_Plugin.json[/b], a small file that lets the Mod Loader update the plugin on its own later on. Without it, the plugin will never update by itself.

If you play on a dedicated server, install the server build of [b]MapExtension_Plugin[/b] in the server [b]Plugins[/b] folder as well so the client and server plugins can communicate with each other.

[line]

[size=4][b]Updates[/b][/size]

Once [b]MapExtension_Plugin.json[/b] sits next to the DLL in your [b]Plugins[/b] folder, the Mod Loader checks for a newer plugin version when the game starts and replaces [b]MapExtension_Plugin.dll[/b] for you.

[b]Important:[/b] the automatic update only replaces the plugin DLL. It does [b]not[/b] touch [b]MapExtensionViewer.html[/b], [b]map-tiles[/b], or [b]map-data[/b], because those live wherever you chose to put them on your PC.

Good news: [b]the map viewer tells you when its payload contract is incompatible.[/b] If the plugin has moved on to a contract the viewer no longer understands, a window opens in the browser page with a direct download link for the new viewer, plus links to the GitHub release and to this mod page. Backward-compatible viewer improvements may not open that window, so install the matching viewer archive manually when a release includes viewer changes.

When that happens:

[list=1]
[*]Download the viewer archive from the link in the window[/*]
[*]Replace your [b]MapExtensionViewer.html[/b], [b]map-tiles[/b], and [b]map-data[/b] with the ones from the archive[/*]
[*]Reload [b]MapExtensionViewer.html[/b] in your browser[/*]
[/list]

Always keep [b]map-tiles[/b] and [b]map-data[/b] next to [b]MapExtensionViewer.html[/b], otherwise the map background or world catalog will not load.

[list]
[*]On a dedicated server, the server build is [b]not[/b] updated automatically: protocol v6 requires you to replace the server [b]MapExtension_Plugin.dll[/b] by hand and update it together with the client build[/*]
[*]Automatic updates can be turned off in the Mod Loader by setting [code]Enabled=0[/code] under the [code][AutoUpdate][/code] section of [b]modloader.ini[/b][/*]
[/list]

